From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: the node program loads V8's startup snapshot

Chromium's V8 reads its startup snapshot from snapshot_blob.bin beside
the program, not from the binary, so the `node` built against it failed
to create an isolate: "Failed to deserialize the V8 snapshot blob".
Electron loads the blob through gin; the node program has to say where
it is itself.
---
 src/node_main.cc | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/node_main.cc b/src/node_main.cc
index 3295121..ab44822 100644
--- a/src/node_main.cc
+++ b/src/node_main.cc
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 // USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.
 
 #include "node.h"
+#include "v8.h"
 #include <cstdio>
 
 #ifdef _WIN32
@@ -94,6 +95,9 @@ int wmain(int argc, wchar_t* wargv[]) {
 // UNIX
 
 int main(int argc, char* argv[]) {
+  // Chromium's V8 keeps its startup snapshot beside the program, in
+  // snapshot_blob.bin, rather than built in.
+  v8::V8::InitializeExternalStartupData(argv[0]);
   return node::Start(argc, argv);
 }
 #endif
